From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: scaled CAPTURE for HEVC and VP9

At 3840x2160 and 60 fps the display's video plane reads 750 MB/s of NV12
and cannot keep up. The HEVC core's second, uncompressed write can be
scaled by 2 or 4 each way while the references stay full size and
compressed, as Amlogic's double_write_mode 4 and 2 do.

A client asks per stream, as the stateful decoder interface has it:
S_SELECTION with the COMPOSE target on CAPTURE, before CAPTURE buffers
exist. The rectangle is kept, and the ratio is the smallest of 1, 2 and
4 whose picture fits it, worked out again from the stream's own visible
size once its headers are parsed. G_FMT reports the scaled size, and
G_SELECTION the visible picture as CROP and COMPOSE_BOUNDS. A client
that never asks gets capture_max_height, off by default.

With a ratio, HEVC and VP9 decode to compressed references at 8-bit too,
CAPTURE is allocated at the scaled size, rounded down, the compressed
buffers at the full one, and HEVC_SAO_CTRL5[23:16] takes 0x33 or 0xff.
VP9 zeroed the scale field on every frame and cleared the 8-bit memory
saving bit its compressed buffers are sized for; both now follow the
session.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
